wizard: FUS RO DOH!
wizard: .[pause=0.5].[pause=0.5].[pause=0.5]No wait, that's not right.
if {HasWizardToken} == 0:
	wizard: You want my autograph? Bah, I do not have time for small tin people.
	wizard: Here, take this meager handout and begone.
	[signal arg="coin_received"]
	set {HasWizardToken} = 1
	set {TokenCount} += 1
elif {WizardRevealed} == 0:
	wizard: ...Wait.
	wizard: [pause=0.3]Hold still, little one.
	wizard: [color=cyan]There's something rattling behind your eyes that isn't gears.[/color]
	wizard: A soul, half-asleep, wrapped around a duty it never chose. How curious, for something built.
	wizard: I am no healer, but I know a dormant Core when I feel one straining against its own shell.
	wizard: [i]That[/i] tree at the edge of town — the one nobody can be bothered to walk around — has roots that answer to the same kind of strain. Go look at it properly this time.
	wizard: And when you're done staring at bark, there's an old pedestal in the house past the square. Wands, colors, a little ritual. It was built to test exactly what's rattling in you.
	wizard: Go on, then. Wake it up before it wakes up angry.
	set {WizardRevealed} = 1
else:
	wizard: The tree, then the pedestal. Don't dawdle — a strained soul doesn't get gentler with time.
[end_timeline]
